Directory Structure
The dataset is organized by scene, with each scene containing consistent sub-directories for images, camera parameters, and ground truth data.
vims_gs/
├── classroom/
│   ├── images/             # High-resolution scene captures
│   ├── sparse/0             # COLMAP camera poses and calibration
│   ├── ground_truth.ply    # LiDAR scan (Ground Truth)
│   └── split.json          # Train/Test partition metadata
├── lounge/
│   ├── images/
│   ├── sparse/0
│   ├── ground_truth.ply
│   └── split.json
└── lobby/
    ├── images/
    ├── sparse/0
    ├── ground_truth.ply
    └── split.json

Data Component Details
1. images/
Contains the raw image files (e.g., .jpg or .png) captured for the specific scene.
2. sparse/0
Contains the camera registration data exported in COLMAP format. This folder typically includes:
cameras.bin: Camera model and intrinsic parameters.
images.bin: Registration info and extrinsic parameters for each image.
points3D.bin: Sparse point cloud generated during SfM.
3. ground_truth.ply
A dense 3D point cloud or mesh generated from a LiDAR scan. 
4. split.json
A JSON file defining the data distribution for machine learning pipelines.

